\begin_body

\begin_layout abstract
In Cuban higher education,
 the planning of academic timetables and the management of teaching workload are key processes for the organization of institutional work.
 At the University of Sancti Spíritus «José Martí Pérez» (UNISS),
 these processes were managed through independent documents and spreadsheets,
 which hindered the updating and control of academic assignments,
 the detection of conflicts among teachers,
 groups and classrooms,
 and the monitoring of the distribution of teaching responsibilities.
 This work develops a web system for the integrated management of teaching timetables (P4) and teaching workload,
 centralizing academic information and linking scheduled teaching activities with the responsibilities assigned to each teacher.
 The solution integrates the management of degree programs,
 curricula,
 subjects and teaching timetables with the recording,
 calculation,
 consultation and monitoring of teaching workload,
 and incorporates functionalities for identifying conflicts and imbalances in the distribution of work.
 The application was developed under the RUP methodology,
 with a technology stack composed of Nuxt.js on the frontend,
 Express.js on the backend and PostgreSQL as the database management system,
 and validates its operation through functional tests and the assessment of specialists and users.
 With this tool,
 it is possible to centralize and organize information,
 improve the control of academic assignments and facilitate decision-making in the academic planning of UNISS,
 being adaptable to other similar university contexts.
\end_layout

